-  "ground_truth_reference_answer": "If a Locational Clearance is denied by the Zoning Administrator, an applicant may file a Motion for Reconsideration before the Local Zoning Board of Adjustment and Appeals (LZBAA). Requirements are: 1) Letter of Reconsideration; 2) Denial Letter; 3) Title/Lease Contract; 4) Site sketch plan with vicinity landmarks; 5) Barangay Council Resolution of No Objection; 6) Locational mapping of neighbor's consent signatories; and 7) Notarized Affidavit of Non-Objection from adjoining property owners. The processing fee is PHP 600.00, and evaluation involves TWG site inspection, committee deliberation, and LZBAA board resolution.",
+  "ground_truth_reference_answer": "Motion for Reconsideration is an appeal against denial of Locational Clearance by the Zoning Administrator. The checklist lists: Letter of Reconsideration; Denial Letter; Order of Payment; Official Receipt; Business Permit Application Form/Building Permit Application Form (for building permit); certified true copy of title(s)/Contract of Lease/Deed of Sale; site sketch with vicinity map and landmarks; Barangay Council Resolution Interposing No Objection; affidavit of non-objection of adjoining property owners; locational mapping of neighbor consent signatories; Affidavit of Undertaking; and Building Permit for a business-permit application.\n\nSecure checklist and pre-evaluation; once documents are complete, obtain the order for the PHP600 processing fee. Submit original and photocopied official receipt with one complete set of documents. The process includes TWG site inspection/evaluation, TWG meeting with the applicant, committee deliberation, and, if approved, resolution and endorsement to OBO or Business Bureau. Claim the endorsement with attached resolution. Non-approved/deferred cases may receive NOC, NOD or disapproval.",
   "queries": {
     "english": "What is the procedure, fee, and requirement checklist to appeal a denied Locational Clearance before the LZBAA?",
